            <ArticleTitle>Sacroiliitis and severe disability due to isotretinoin therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>985-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00296-009-1014-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of acute sacroiliitis with severe disability after only 3 weeks of isotretinoin therapy with graduate reduction of pain, limitation and muscle incompetence after discontinuation of the drug and ACTH-depo injection and Ethodolac therapy. Naranjo probability scale indicated a probable relationship between isotretinoin therapy and bilateral sacroiliitis. We discussed possible mechanisms of sacroiliitis and disability due to isotretinoin treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
